<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">12 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 12 September, from 490 BCE to 1962.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/athens" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/athens.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">490 BCE <span class="tih-ago">1,536 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Athenians defeat the Persians at Marathon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By the traditional date, the Athenians and Plataeans charged and routed the Persian landing force at Marathon. The legend of a runner carrying news to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> inspired the modern marathon race.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1213">1213 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">813 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Simon de Montfort defeats and kills Peter II of Aragon at Muret</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a> under Simon de Montfort routed a larger army of Aragon and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> at Muret, killing King Peter II. The defeat ended Aragonese hopes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/languedoc">Languedoc</a> and opened it to northern French rule.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1683">1683 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">343 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John III Sobieski relieves the siege of Vienna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A relief army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> III Sobieski of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> routed the Ottoman forces besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, ending with a great charge of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-hussars">Polish hussars</a>. The Ottoman advance into central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> was halted for good.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-hussars">Polish hussars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1848">1848 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Switzerland adopts its federal constitution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Swiss Diet declared the new federal constitution accepted, turning a loose league of cantons into a federal state with a two-chamber parliament. Its framework still underpins <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> today.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1962">1962 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kennedy tells Rice University 'we choose to go to the Moon'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a speech at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">Rice</a> University in Houston, John F. Kennedy committed America to a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a> landing that decade, 'not because they are easy, but because they are hard'. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> 11 landed seven years later.</p></div></li></ol>
